  "sourceType": "MANUAL",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Present Worth, Loans, and Repayments",
    "description": "Apply simple interest to future dues, loan settlement, part payments, down payments, and borrowing/lending decisions.",
    "teachingApproach": "Use a cash-flow timeline: what is paid now, what principal remains active, and for how long? Present worth runs the amount factor backward; loan payoff runs it forward. Practice should target the common mistake of charging interest on money that has already been paid.",
    "targetDurationMinutes": 30,
    "sourceScope": "R.S. Aggarwal, Quantitative Aptitude for Competitive Examinations, Chapter 22, Simple Interest (printed pp. 641–662). Approved scope: Teach present worth through A=P(1+RT/100), ordinary loan repayment, part-payment timelines, cash down payments where only the unpaid balance earns interest, net gain from borrowing at one rate and lending at another, and rate recovery from a known repayment amount. Keep the source's simple-interest treatment explicit and separate principal from accumulated interest at every stage."
  },
  "startNodeId": "start",
  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Present Worth, Loans, and Repayments\n\nApply simple interest to future dues, loan settlement, part payments, down payments, and borrowing/lending decisions.\n\nWe will build the idea with small numbers first, then move into the exam-style patterns from the chapter.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Present worth asks: what principal today will grow to a known future amount under simple interest? Use A = P(1+RT/100) and divide by the growth factor.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "₹1320 due in 2 years at 5% has factor 1.10, so its present worth is 1320/1.10 = ₹1200.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
